                                        "entry_id": "182733bb-3e70-30f7-ab76-db9ee4faf372",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The abode of the gods at the center of the universe in Hindu, Jain, and Buddhist traditions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e6b4cc5-3d46-4cc5-b42a-dd1af9180730",
                                                "sense_id": "652a2f01-cec3-3854-b510-fab1baeb0d63",
                                                "text": "2003, J. Dina Bagdel, John C. Huntington Buddhist Cosmology: Environment of Meditative Transformation: Mount Meru, John C. Huntington, Dina Bangdel, Robert A. F. Thurman, The Circle of Bliss: Buddhist Meditational Art, page 66,\nBuddhist realizations and transformations take place in a sacred meditational space known as Mount Meru, or Sumeru. In Western-language literature, the Mount Meru system is often construed as the \"Buddhist universe,\" but this description is misleading as it implies a singular phenomenon. The Mount Meru system is indeed an expression of Buddhist cosmology, but it describes structure of the cosmos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "286fc7ab-9e66-4c04-ab13-2e0e5b9fab2f",
                                                "sense_id": "652a2f01-cec3-3854-b510-fab1baeb0d63",
                                                "text": "2013, Eric Huntington, Portrait of a Landscape: Depictions of the Meru Cosmos in Buddhist Art & Culture, Dissertation, University of Chicago."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
